.Dd October 9, 2026
.Dt BSDTIMECTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BSDTimectl
.Nd operator CLI for the system.Time capability
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm get
.Nm Cm set Ar epoch Ns Op . Ns Ar nsec
.Nm Cm adjust Ar delta
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and, with authority, sets the system wall clock through the
.Dq system.Time
capability provider
.Pq Xr BSDTime 8 .
.Bl -tag -width adjust
.It Cm get
Print
.Dv CLOCK_REALTIME
as
.Ar seconds . Ns Ar nanoseconds .
.It Cm set Ar epoch Ns Op . Ns Ar nsec
Step the clock to an absolute time.
Fails with
.Er EPERM
unless the caller's label is granted set authority in
.Xr BSDTime 8 Ns 's
.Pa time.conf .
.It Cm adjust Ar delta
Slew the clock by a signed delta
.Pq Xr adjtime 2 ,
printing the correction that was still pending.
The argument has the form
.Li [-]sec[.usec] ;
the optional suffix is an integer microsecond count from 0 through 999999.
For example,
.Li -2.345678
requests a negative correction of two seconds and 345678 microseconds.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libtimecmp 3 ,
.Xr BSDTime 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
